course: dictionary
lesson: 14203
title: Moved: a new place or a strong feeling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word moved has more than one meaning, so use the words around it as clues. Moved is the past form of move, so it tells you something has already happened: «She moved the chair to the window.» She already carried the chair to a different place.
explain: Moved can also mean a family went to live in a new home: «We moved to Leeds last summer.» The words Leeds and summer are clues. Try your meaning in the sentence: «We went to live in Leeds last summer» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Moved can also describe a feeling. «The song moved the whole audience to tears.» Tears and a song are clues that the feeling is strong. Here moved means touched by strong feelings, not a change of place.
fact: Moved is the past form of move, so it describes an action that is already finished.
fact: «Moved» can mean went to live in a new home, as in «We moved house in May.»
fact: «Moved» can mean touched by strong feelings, as in «The music moved me.»
fact: When moved describes a person, as in «She was moved by the letter», it shows a deep feeling.
fact: The words around moved, such as home, town, tears or music, show you which meaning is right.
exercise: «Sam moved the books onto the top shelf.» What does moved mean here? | Read them quickly | *Carried them to a different place | Sold them at a shop | Felt very sad about the books
exercise: «The Carters moved to a new town last year.» What does moved mean? | Forgot the old town | Stayed in the same house all their lives | *Went to live in a new home | Ran a race in the new town
exercise: «The choir sang so beautifully that Grandma was moved.» What does moved mean here? | Asked to leave the room | Carried away by a strong wind | Dancing around the room | *Touched by strong feelings
test: «We moved the old sofa into the garage.» What did we do to the sofa? | Threw it away | Sat on it all day | Painted it | *Carried it to another place
test: «The film was so sad that the whole class was moved.» What does moved mean? | Ran outside to play | *Touched and full of strong feelings | Got up and left the room | Fell fast asleep
exam: «After the flood, the family moved away from the village.» What does moved mean here, and which words are the clue? | Ate lunch, because after is the clue | Sang loudly, because family is the clue | Ran fast from the water, because flood is the clue | *Went to live somewhere else, because away and village are the clues
